sxml-xslt-test run - Run test cases and report them

Usage: sxml-xslt-test run [--catalog=FILE] [--test-set=NAME] [--format=FORMAT] [TEST-LIST]

Plans each selected test case's transformation (principal
stylesheet or package, secondary modules, static and stylesheet
parameters, global context item, invocation, delivery) and checks
that its assertions are known, then reports it: until sxml
implements XSLT every applicable test case is "not run" with the
reason "XSLT not implemented". Writes each test case that failed
or ended in error, counts per test set and a "total:" line;
--format=json writes every test case and how many are in the D95
scope. The selection is the test cases of TEST-LIST, those of the
test set --test-set names, or with neither every test case of the
catalog. Exits 1 when a test case failed or ended in error, 3 when
a file cannot be read.

Options:
  -h, --help           Show this help and exit
      --catalog=FILE   The catalog.xml of the suite (default: third_party/xslt40-test/catalog.xml)
      --test-set=NAME  Run every test case of one test set
      --format=FORMAT  The form of the report (one of: text, json; default: text)

Arguments:
  TEST-LIST  File naming test cases, one '<test-set> <test-case>' per line

Examples:
  sxml-xslt-test run tests/xslt/slice.txt
  sxml-xslt-test run --test-set=apply-templates
  sxml-xslt-test run --format=json > report.json
